From 1a454ad6a1c0c6f88d3d757a471d5ef85c60bb92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:52:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Ignore locally installed agent tooling

`npx skills add higgsfield-ai/skills` writes ~110 files of third-party
skill definitions into .agents/, plus editor-local settings under
.claude/ and a skills-lock.json. None of it is MINIMEE application code,
and the repo may be migrated to another host, so keep it untracked.
---
 .gitignore | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 0aeb9c8..a921f22 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -10,3 +10,11 @@ vite.config.js
 vite.config.d.ts
 vitest.config.js
 vitest.config.d.ts
+
+# Agent tooling installed locally by `npx skills add` (Higgsfield skills and
+# friends). These are third-party skill definitions and machine-local editor
+# settings, not part of the MINIMEE product — keep them out of the repo so a
+# migration elsewhere carries application code only.
+.agents/
+.claude/
+skills-lock.json
-- 
